KONOHAGAKURE — FOREHEAD PROTECTOR (HEADBAND) ISSUANCE RECORD

The Konoha forehead protector bears the engraved leaf spiral of the Hidden Leaf and is issued upon successful Academy graduation. It is the mark of a full shinobi of the village.

Issuance log (sample entries):
- Uzumaki, Naruto — issued at graduation by instructor Iruka Umino (personally gifted). Worn on the forehead.
- Nara, Shikamaru — issued at graduation. Worn on left arm.
- Hyuga, Hinata — issued at graduation. Worn around neck.
- Inuzuka, Kiba — issued at graduation.

Conditions of issuance:
- The headband signifies loyalty to the village. Defacing the plate with a slash across the leaf symbol denotes severance of ties (missing-nin) and is a serious matter.
- Lost or damaged headbands must be reported to the Administration Building for reissue.

Recorded by the Ninja Registration Desk.
